# images.db - which image formats each PS1 disc uses, and which compression.
# Written by psx_tim_check.py (checker v2); separate from db.py,
# keyed the same way.
#
# Key:   MD5 over the raw 2352-byte sectors of track 1, as in db.py's disc_by_md5.
#        The comment after each entry is the title from db.py.
# Value: {format: {'uncompressed': n, 'compressed': {scheme: n}}}
#        'uncompressed': images of that format found as they are, every occurrence
#                        counted, duplicates included; each confirmed by parsing it.
#        'compressed':   images a known decompressor produced, per compression scheme.
#                        This is a LOWER BOUND: only an image at the very start of a
#                        compressed stream is seen.
#        Zero counts and empty formats are left out. A disc with no images at all
#        has no entry; it is listed in images.db.done, the log of scanned images.
#        No entry, or no 'compressed', does not mean the disc has no compressed
#        images: it may use a scheme not in this list, or its own image format.
#
# Image formats:
#   tim   Sony TIM (ID 10h): pixel block with optional CLUT
#   pxl   Sony PXL (ID 11h/12h, flags 0/1): pixel block only; its CLT palettes are not counted
#   bs    MDEC picture, BS v1/v2/v3 (also video frames stored in ordinary files)
#   jpeg  JPEG (JFIF/EXIF/raw): SOI + valid segment chain with SOF and SOS
#   gif   GIF87a/GIF89a
#   png   PNG
#   bmp   Windows/OS2 bitmap
#   pcx   ZSoft PCX
#   tiff  TIFF (II/MM)
#   tga   Targa 2.0 (by its footer; Targa 1.0 files have no signature and are not counted)
#   ilbm  IFF ILBM/PBM (Amiga/Deluxe Paint)
#
# Compression schemes (LZSS: 4 KB window, match length 3-18, one flag byte per 8
# items; the ring buffer's fill byte (0x00 or 0x20) is probed too but can't be told
# apart at a stream start, so it is not part of the name).
# How a match's two bytes hold the 12-bit offset and the 4-bit length:
#   layout A  byte0 = offset low 8 bits, byte1 = (offset high 4 bits) << 4 | (length - 3)
#   layout B  byte0 = (length - 3) << 4 | offset high 4 bits, byte1 = offset low 8 bits
#   layout C  byte0 = offset low 8 bits, byte1 = (length - 3) << 4 | offset high 4 bits
#
#   gzip                    gzip stream (1F 8B 08 ...), inflated with zlib
#   zlib                    zlib stream (78 01/5E/9C/DA, valid header checksum)
#   lzss-okumura            Okumura's LZSS.C (ring, low-first, 1 = literal, layout A); Squaresoft .LZS: FF7, FF8, Chrono Cross
#   lzss-dist+0-A-lsb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+1-A-lsb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-ring-A-lsb-lit0    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+0-A-lsb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+1-A-lsb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-ring-A-msb-lit1    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+0-A-msb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+1-A-msb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-ring-A-msb-lit0    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+0-A-msb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-dist+1-A-msb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout A
#   lzss-ring-B-lsb-lit1    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+0-B-lsb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+1-B-lsb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-ring-B-lsb-lit0    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+0-B-lsb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+1-B-lsb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-ring-B-msb-lit1    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+0-B-msb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+1-B-msb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-ring-B-msb-lit0    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+0-B-msb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-dist+1-B-msb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout B
#   lzss-ring-C-lsb-lit1    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+0-C-lsb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+1-C-lsb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits low-first, 1 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-ring-C-lsb-lit0    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+0-C-lsb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+1-C-lsb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits low-first, 0 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-ring-C-msb-lit1    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+0-C-msb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+1-C-msb-lit1  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits high-first, 1 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-ring-C-msb-lit0    match = absolute position in a 4 KB ring buffer (writes start at 0xFEE); flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+0-C-msb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position; flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-dist+1-C-msb-lit0  match = distance back from the current output position + 1; flag bits high-first, 0 = literal; layout C
#   lzss-ambiguous          surely one of the LZSS variants above (it decodes into a confirmed image), but more than one variant does, so which can't be told
